              "version": "3.1"
            },
            "format": "CVSS"
          }
        ],
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "A flaw was found in GNU Coreutils. The sort utility's begfield() function is vulnerable to a heap buffer under-read. The program may access memory outside the allocated buffer if a user runs a crafted command using the traditional key format. A malicious input could lead to a crash or leak sensitive data."
          }
        ],
